articles.content_en:
Article 1 Whoever commits sexual intercourse with a female child under the age of fourteen shall be given a severe punishment in accordance with the provisions of Paragraph 2 of Article 236 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China. Under any of the following circumstances, a relatively heavier range of severe punishment shall apply:
(1) a person with special duties commits the act;
(2) the act is committed by means of violence, coercion, or the like;
(3) the act is committed by intruding into a residence or a student dormitory;
(4) the victim is a left-behind female child in rural areas, a victim with severe disability or mental retardation;
(5) using other minors to lure, introduce, or coerce the victim;
(6) having been previously sentenced to punishment for rape or indecent assault.
Where the victim is a female minor aged fourteen or above, and the act of rape falls under any of the circumstances specified in items (1), (3) to (6) of the preceding paragraph, or causes the victim to suffer minor injury, contract serious sexually transmitted diseases such as syphilis or gonorrhea, the perpetrator shall be convicted and given a severe punishment in accordance with the provisions of Paragraph 1 of Article 236 of the Criminal Law.

Article 2 Rape of a female minor aged fourteen or above or sexual intercourse with a female child under the age of fourteen, under any of the following circumstances, shall be deemed as the 'heinous circumstances of rape of a woman or sexual intercourse with a female child' provided in Item (1) of Paragraph 3 of Article 236 of the Criminal Law:
(1) a person with special duties commits rape or sexual intercourse multiple times;
(2) there are acts of severe torture or humiliation;
(3) illegally detaining the victim or using drugs to lure or control the victim;
(4) repeatedly using other minors to lure, introduce, or coerce the victim;
(5) committing rape or sexual intercourse over a long period;
(6) causing pregnancy of a victim with mental retardation through sexual intercourse;
(7) making videos, photos or other image materials of the rape or sexual intercourse process or the victim's intimate body parts, using such materials to coerce the victim into rape or sexual intercourse, or causing such materials to be disseminated to multiple persons, thereby exposing the victim's identity;
(8) other heinous circumstances.

Article 3 Sexual intercourse with a female child under the age of fourteen, under any of the following circumstances, shall be deemed as 'causing injury to a female child' provided in Item (5) of Paragraph 3 of Article 236 of the Criminal Law:
(1) causing minor injury to the female child;
(2) causing the female child to contract serious sexually transmitted diseases such as syphilis or gonorrhea;
(3) other circumstances causing injury to the physical and mental health of the female child.

Article 5 A person with special duties towards a female minor aged fourteen or above but under the age of sixteen who has sexual relations with such female minor, under any of the following circumstances, shall be deemed as having 'heinous circumstances' as provided in Article 236a of the Criminal Law:
(1) having sexual relations over a long period;
(2) having sexual relations with multiple victims;
(3) causing the victim to contract HIV or serious sexually transmitted diseases such as syphilis or gonorrhea;
(4) making videos, photos or other image materials of the sexual relations process or the victim's intimate body parts, causing such materials to be disseminated to multiple persons, thereby exposing the victim's identity;
(5) other heinous circumstances.

Article 7 Indecent assault on a child, under any of the following circumstances, shall be deemed as 'causing injury to the child or other serious consequences' provided in Item (3) of Paragraph 3 of Article 237 of the Criminal Law:
(1) causing the child to suffer minor injury or above;
(2) causing the child to self-harm or commit suicide;
(3) other circumstances causing injury or other serious consequences to the child's physical and mental health.

Article 8 Indecent assault on a child, under any of the following circumstances, shall be deemed as 'heinous means of indecency or other heinous circumstances' provided in Item (4) of Paragraph 3 of Article 237 of the Criminal Law:
(1) committing indecency by inserting the genital organ into the anus or oral cavity, or by inserting body parts other than the genital organ or objects into the victim's genital organ or anus;
(2) there are acts of severe torture or humiliation;
(3) making videos, photos or other image materials of the indecent assault process or the victim's intimate body parts, using such materials to coerce the victim into indecent assault, or causing such materials to be disseminated to multiple persons, thereby exposing the victim's identity;
(4) committing indecency by other heinous means or having other heinous circumstances.
